.TH OS 3 "2026" "y-- standard library" "y-- Library Reference"
.SH NAME
Os \- filesystem and process utilities
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B Os
module provides filesystem operations (create, remove, rename, copy,
inspect files and directories), process utilities (current directory,
environment variables), and shell command execution.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.SS Make
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
none() Make(directory: string(), filename: string())
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Creates an empty file at directory/filename.
Raises \fBPermissionError\fR if the file cannot be created.
.TP
\fBERRORS\fR
\fBArgumentError\fR, \fBPermissionError\fR
.SS Remove
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
none() Remove(path: string())
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Deletes the file at path using C \fBstd::remove\fR.
Raises \fBPermissionError\fR on failure.
.TP
\fBERRORS\fR
\fBArgumentError\fR, \fBPermissionError\fR
.SS Exists
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
bool() Exists(directory: string(), filename: string())
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Returns true if directory/filename is a readable file, false otherwise.
.TP
\fBERRORS\fR
\fBArgumentError\fR
.SS ListNames
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
list() ListNames(path: string())
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
If path is a directory: returns a list of entry names.
If path is a regular file: returns a list of lines.
Raises \fBFileNotFoundError\fR if path does not exist.
.TP
\fBERRORS\fR
\fBArgumentError\fR, \fBFileNotFoundError\fR
.SS MkDir
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
none() MkDir(path: string())
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Creates path and any missing parent directories.
Silently succeeds if directory already exists.
.TP
\fBERRORS\fR
\fBArgumentError\fR
.SS RmDir
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
none() RmDir(path: string(), recursive: bool() = false)
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Removes directory at path.
When recursive is true, removes directory and all contents.
.TP
\fBERRORS\fR
\fBArgumentError\fR (0 or >2 args)
.SS Cwd
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
string() Cwd()
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Returns the current working directory as an absolute path string.
.SS Cd
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
none() Cd(path: string())
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Changes the working directory to path.
Raises \fBFileNotFoundError\fR if path does not exist.
.TP
\fBERRORS\fR
\fBArgumentError\fR, \fBFileNotFoundError\fR
.SS Rename
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
none() Rename(old: string(), new: string())
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Renames or moves the file/directory at old to new.
Raises \fBPermissionError\fR on failure.
.TP
\fBERRORS\fR
\fBArgumentError\fR, \fBPermissionError\fR
.SS Env
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
string() Env(name: string())
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Returns the value of the named environment variable, or none() if not set.
.TP
\fBERRORS\fR
\fBArgumentError\fR
.SS SetEnv
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
none() SetEnv(name: string(), value: string())
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Sets environment variable name to value (overwriting any existing value).
.SS Copy
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
none() Copy(src: string(), dst: string())
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Copies src to dst, overwriting dst if it exists.
.SS FileSize
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
int() FileSize(path: string())
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Returns the size of the file at path in bytes.
.SS IsDir
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
bool() IsDir(path: string())
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Returns true if path is an existing directory.
.SS IsFile
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
bool() IsFile(path: string())
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Returns true if path is an existing regular file.
.SS Direct
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
int() Direct(command: string(), file: string())
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Runs command in the shell, redirecting stdout and stderr to file.
Returns the exit status code.
.SS Console
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
int() Console(command: string())
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Runs command via std::system, output goes to the terminal.
Returns exit status code.
.TP
\fBERRORS\fR
\fBArgumentError\fR
.SS Exec
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
string() Exec(command: string())
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Runs command via popen and captures stdout as a string.
Raises \fBRuntimeError\fR if popen fails.
.TP
\fBERRORS\fR
\fBArgumentError\fR, \fBRuntimeError\fR
.SH "SEE ALSO"
FileStream(3), System(3)
